$DIR/main.p:27:3: p holds a view of c (&c, line 25), which was moved into consume (its parameter takes a Conn by value) at line 26, so p can no longer be used here
    p looks at memory that c owns, without owning it: the view was made by &c at
    line 25. A view of an owner held in a local variable may be used only while
    the variable keeps the value the view was made from. At line 26 c was moved
    into consume (its parameter takes a Conn by value), so the view may look at
    memory that was released, or at a value that now belongs to something else.
    Go keeps memory alive for as long as any pointer refers to it. Plutonium has
    no garbage collector: an owner releases its memory when it is dropped, so a
    view must not be used after the value it looks at has gone.
    Use p before line 26, or move c only after the last use of p
    Or move a copy at line 26, so that c keeps its value:
        c.Clone()
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3313" for a longer explanation)

